<p class="legal-date">Last updated October 20, 2026</p>

<p>8bitNYC ("we", "us") runs 8bit.nyc, a pixel map of New York City that shows the day's events. This policy explains what information we collect when you use the site, why, and the choices you have.</p>

<h3>Where the listings come from</h3>
<p>We do not collect the event listings from you. Every event on the map comes from outside sources, including NYC.gov Events and NYC Parks, NYC Open Data street event permits, Luma, Ticketmaster, SeatGeek, Artwrld and venues' own calendars. When you open a listing, buy a ticket or follow a link, you leave our site and that service's own privacy policy applies.</p>

<h3>What we collect</h3>
<ul>
  <li><b>Messages you send us.</b> If you use the contact form, we receive your name, email address, the topic you picked and your message, and keep them in our email inboxes so we can reply.</li>
  <li><b>Analytics.</b> We use Google Analytics to understand how many people visit and which parts of the map they use. It sets cookies and collects information such as pages viewed, device and browser type, referring site and approximate location (city level). Google may process this information on its servers in the United States. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">how Google uses data from sites that use its services</a>.</li>
  <li><b>Hosting and security.</b> The site runs on Cloudflare. Cloudflare processes your IP address and basic request details to deliver pages, block abuse and work out which country you are visiting from, so we know whether to ask for cookie consent.</li>
  <li><b>Cookies we set ourselves.</b> One remembers that you entered the preview password, and one remembers your cookie choice if we asked you for it. Neither is used for tracking.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not ask for accounts, payment details or precise location, and we do not knowingly collect information about children under 13.</p>

<h3>Advertising</h3>
<p>The banner next to the header holds ads and featured events that we sell directly to advertisers. These are labeled as ads. We do not currently use third-party ad networks or ad tracking cookies. Clicking an ad takes you to the advertiser's site, where their privacy policy applies. If we add an ad partner that uses cookies, we will update this policy and, where the law requires it, ask for your consent first.</p>

<h3>How we use information</h3>
<ul>
  <li>To answer your messages, including ad and event inquiries.</li>
  <li>To understand and improve how the site is used.</li>
  <li>To keep the site running and secure.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it with anyone except the service providers named above (Google, Cloudflare and our email providers), when the law requires it, or to protect our rights or the safety of others.</p>

<h3>Visitors in the EU, EEA, UK and Switzerland</h3>
<p>If you visit from these regions, Google Analytics stays off until you accept analytics cookies in the banner, and you can change your choice at any time from Cookie Settings in the menu. Our legal bases are your consent (analytics), our legitimate interest in running and securing the site (hosting and security) and our legitimate interest in replying to you (contact messages). You have the right to access, correct or delete your information, to object to or restrict its use, to data portability, to withdraw consent at any time, and to complain to your local data protection authority. Your information is processed in the United States, and our providers use safeguards such as Standard Contractual Clauses for these transfers.</p>

<h3>Visitors in California and other US states</h3>
<p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to know what personal information we hold about you, to ask us to delete or correct it, and to opt out of its sale or use for targeted advertising. We do not sell personal information or use it for targeted advertising. To limit analytics, you can block cookies in your browser or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.</p>

<h3>How long we keep it</h3>
<p>Contact messages are kept as long as needed to deal with them and then for a reasonable period for our records. Google Analytics data is kept for up to 14 months. Cloudflare keeps request logs for a short period under its own policy.</p>

<h3>Changes</h3>
<p>If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top. Significant changes will be noted on the site.</p>

<h3>Contact</h3>
<p>For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:info@8bit.nyc">info@8bit.nyc</a>.</p>
